        <section class="activity-section" id="trusts">
            <div class="activity-wrap">
                <header class="activity-section-header">
                    <div>
                        <span class="activity-eyebrow">The Institutional Foundation</span>
                        <h2>Four trusts, each answering a distinct need</h2>
                    </div>
                    <p>Together, these institutions carry the Mission across school and higher education, support for boys, and the preservation of Bhaiyaji’s spiritual knowledge.</p>
                </header>

                <div class="trust-grid">
                    <article class="trust-card" id="swami-vivekanand-trust">
                        <span class="anchor-alias" id="school-education" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <div class="trust-card-top"><span class="trust-number">01</span><span class="trust-year">Established 10 June 1996</span></div>
                        <h3>Swami Vivekanand Students’ Welfare Charitable Trust</h3>
                        <div class="trust-focus">School education and lifelong formation for girls</div>
                        <p>Created so that financial hardship would not end a deserving girl’s education, the Trust combines scholarship support with mentorship, Sanskar, confidence-building and continued personal guidance.</p>
                        <div class="trust-tags"><span>School scholarships</span><span>Girls’ education</span><span>Mentorship</span><span>Sanskar</span></div>
                    </article>

                    <article class="trust-card" id="maa-shardamani-trust">
                        <span class="anchor-alias" id="higher-education" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <div class="trust-card-top"><span class="trust-number">02</span><span class="trust-year">Established 28 March 2001</span></div>
                        <h3>Maa Shardamani Trust</h3>
                        <div class="trust-focus">Higher education for young women</div>
                        <p>School completion should not become the end of aspiration. Maa Shardamani Trust extends support into college and advanced study, helping young women pursue professional and academic futures with confidence.</p>
                        <div class="trust-tags"><span>College scholarships</span><span>Higher education</span><span>Academic continuity</span></div>
                    </article>

                    <article class="trust-card" id="gyan-ganga-mission">
                        <div class="trust-card-top"><span class="trust-number">03</span><span class="trust-year">Established 16 April 2003</span></div>
                        <h3>Nandkishore Sharda Gyan Ganga Mission</h3>
                        <div class="trust-focus">Spiritual literature and the continuity of knowledge</div>
                        <p>Founded by Maa Basanti and Madhu Maa, the Mission preserves, publishes and freely shares Bhaiyaji’s spiritual knowledge, reflections and personal writings so that future generations can encounter them in their original spirit.</p>
                        <div class="trust-tags"><span>Publications</span><span>Free distribution</span><span>Spiritual legacy</span><span>Archives</span></div>
                    </article>

                    <article class="trust-card" id="adhyatm-kendra">
                        <span class="anchor-alias" id="boys-education" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <div class="trust-card-top"><span class="trust-number">04</span><span class="trust-year">Established 2010</span></div>
                        <h3>Gyanyogi Shri Nandkishore Sharda Adhyatm Kendra</h3>
                        <div class="trust-focus">Education, mentorship and spiritual grounding for boys</div>
                        <p>Established after families expressed that their sons also faced interrupted education, the Kendra supports deserving boys through demanding courses and provides the steady guidance needed beyond financial assistance.</p>
                        <div class="trust-tags"><span>Education for boys</span><span>Professional courses</span><span>Mentorship</span><span>Adhyatm</span></div>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </div>
